# TypeScript and React

- Functional components and hooks only. Type props with an interface. Do not use classes or `React.FC`.
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes. Do not add enums; use a union or a const map.
- Name booleans with `is`, `has`, or `can` (`isLoading`, `hasError`).
- Use the `function` keyword for helpers. Always use curly braces on conditionals.
- Named exports. One component per file, with its props interface in that file.
- Put reusable state in `src/hooks`. Keep pages in `src/pages` and shared UI in `src/components`.
- New directories use lowercase kebab-case (`components/lesson-editor`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
export const Card: React.FC<{ title: string }> = ({ title }) => <h2>{title}</h2>

// ✅ GOOD
interface CardProps {
  title: string
}

export function Card({ title }: CardProps) {
  return <h2>{title}</h2>
}
```
